### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###
### TRANSCRIPT ANALYSIS API — Michael's ML Pipeline
###
### These endpoints run the full 5-model NLP pipeline (cp, le, ed, inc, ius)
### on uploaded transcript xlsx files. The pipeline:
###   1. Reads the xlsx (columns: speaker, text)
###   2. Filters to Interviewer sentences only
###   3. Splits multi-sentence utterances into individual sentences
###   4. Sends each sentence to all 5 NLP models for scoring
###   5. Ranks sentences by pred_score, selects top_n per model
###   6. Builds context windows around each top sentence
###   7. Saves results to: xlsx file on disk, transcript_analysis_log table (JSON + xlsx binary),
###      and sentence_prediction table (one row per sentence per model, SQL-queryable)
###
### Input file requirements:
###   - Format: xlsx
###   - Required columns: [speaker, text]
###   - Speaker values: "Interviewer" (scored), "Patient" (not scored)
###
### Output: JSON response with per-model results + xlsx file for download
###
### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Test file path — change this to match your local file location
@transcript_file = /Users/choih2/Documents/GitHub/Graciela_Lab_Collab/prostate_cancer_project/AI_physician_patient_communication/data/input/Input_Keystrokes REC 001 (SID 10).xlsx
@transcript_file_2 = /Users/choih2/Documents/GitHub/Graciela_Lab_Collab/prostate_cancer_project/AI_physician_patient_communication/data/input/Input_Keystrokes REC001 (SID 14).xlsx


############################################################
### TRANSCRIPT-1. Single File Analysis
###
### Analyze one xlsx transcript file through the full ML pipeline.
###
### Parameters (multipart form-data):
###   file           — The xlsx file to analyze (required)
###   top_n          — Number of highest-scoring sentences per model (default: 0 = all)
###                    Example: top_n=5 returns top 5 sentences per model
###   context_window — Number of surrounding sentences for context (default: 3)
###                    Example: context_window=3 gives 3 before + target + 3 after
###
### The patient_id is derived from the filename:
###   "Input_Keystrokes REC 001 (SID 10).xlsx" → patient_id = "SID_10"
###
### Response includes:
###   - patient_id, total_sentences, parameters used
###   - models: { cp: [...], le: [...], ed: [...], inc: [...], ius: [...] }
###     Each model array contains top_n sentence objects with:
###       name, index, i, i2, speaker, text, .pred_1, context
###
### Results are automatically saved to:
###   - Disk: /app/uploads/{patient_id}_predictions.xlsx
###   - DB table: transcript_analysis_log (JSON blob + xlsx binary)
###   - DB table: sentence_prediction (individual rows, SQL-queryable)
############################################################
POST {{base}}/api/transcript/analyze
X-API-Key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=transcript_boundary

--transcript_boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="Input_Keystrokes REC 001 (SID 10).xlsx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

< {{transcript_file}}
--transcript_boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="top_n"

5
--transcript_boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="context_window"

3
--transcript_boundary--


############################################################
### TRANSCRIPT-1b. Single File Analysis — All Sentences (top_n=0)
###
### Same as above but returns ALL scored sentences (no top_n filtering).
### Useful for comprehensive analysis or when you need every prediction.
### Warning: produces many more rows in the response and DB.
############################################################
POST {{base}}/api/transcript/analyze
X-API-Key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=transcript_boundary_all

--transcript_boundary_all
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="Input_Keystrokes REC 001 (SID 10).xlsx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

< {{transcript_file}}
--transcript_boundary_all
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="top_n"

0
--transcript_boundary_all
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="context_window"

3
--transcript_boundary_all--


############################################################
### TRANSCRIPT-2. Batch Analysis (Multiple Files)
###
### Analyze multiple xlsx files in a single request.
### Each file is processed independently with per-file error handling
### (one file failing does not block others).
###
### Parameters (multipart form-data):
###   files          — Multiple xlsx files (use "files" key for each)
###   top_n          — Applied to all files in the batch
###   context_window — Applied to all files in the batch
###
### Response: array of per-file results, each containing the same
### structure as the single-file endpoint.
############################################################
POST {{base}}/api/transcript/analyze-batch
X-API-Key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=batch_boundary

--batch_boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="Input_Keystrokes REC 001 (SID 10).xlsx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

< {{transcript_file}}
--batch_boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="Input_Keystrokes REC001 (SID 14).xlsx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

< {{transcript_file_2}}
--batch_boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="top_n"

5
--batch_boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="context_window"

3
--batch_boundary--


############################################################
### TRANSCRIPT-3. Download Results — Single Patient (xlsx)
###
### Download the prediction results as an xlsx file for one patient.
###
### The xlsx contains 5 sheets (one per NLP model: cp, inc, ed, ius, le).
### Each sheet has columns: name, index, i, i2, speaker, text, .pred_1, context
###
### Lookup order:
###   1. Disk: /app/uploads/{patient_id}_predictions.xlsx
###   2. DB fallback: reads xlsx_data from transcript_analysis_log
###      (useful if the container was restarted and disk files were lost)
############################################################
GET {{base}}/api/transcript/download/SID_10
X-API-Key: {{api_key}}


############################################################
### TRANSCRIPT-3b. Download Results — Batch (zip)
###
### Download results for multiple patients as a single zip file.
### Each patient's xlsx is included in the zip archive.
###
### Query parameter:
###   patient_ids — Comma-separated list of patient IDs
###
### Falls back to DB if disk files are missing.
############################################################
GET {{base}}/api/transcript/download-batch?patient_ids=SID_10,SID_14
X-API-Key: {{api_key}}


############################################################
### TRANSCRIPT-4. Analysis History — Paginated
###
### View all past analysis runs for a patient, sorted newest first.
###
### URL path parameter:
###   patient_id — The patient to query (e.g., "SID_10")
###
### Query parameters:
###   page — Page number, 1-based (default: 1)
###   size — Items per page (default: 20)
###
### Response:
###   { items: [...], total, page, size, pages }
###   Each item: { id, patient_id, total_sentences, top_n, context_window,
###                source_filename, analyzed_at }
###
### Use the "id" field from history items as "analysis_id" in the
### predictions endpoint to query a specific analysis run.
############################################################
GET {{base}}/api/transcript/history/SID_10
X-API-Key: {{api_key}}

###
# History with pagination (page 1, 5 items per page)
GET {{base}}/api/transcript/history/SID_10?page=1&size=5
X-API-Key: {{api_key}}


############################################################
### TRANSCRIPT-5. Query Sentence-Level Predictions (API)
###
### Retrieve individual sentence predictions stored in the
### sentence_prediction table. Each row represents one sentence
### scored by one NLP model.
###
### URL path parameter:
###   patient_id — The patient to query (e.g., "SID_10")
###
### Query parameters (all optional):
###   model       — Filter by NLP model: cp, inc, ed, ius, or le
###   top_n       — Return only the top N highest-scoring per model
###   analysis_id — Query a specific analysis run (from /history endpoint)
###                  Default: latest analysis run for the patient
###   min_score   — Minimum pred_score threshold (0.0–1.0)
###
### Response:
###   { patient_id, analysis_id, total, predictions: [...] }
###   Each prediction: { model, sentence_index, utterance_index,
###     sentence_in_utterance, speaker, sentence_text, pred_score, context }
###
### Column mapping (xlsx → API response):
###   xlsx column    API field                Description
###   -----------    ---------                -----------
###   (sheet name)   model                    NLP model (cp/inc/ed/ius/le)
###   name           (patient_id in URL)      Patient identifier
###   index          sentence_index           Global sentence number (1-based)
###   i              utterance_index          Utterance number from transcript
###   i2             sentence_in_utterance    Sentence position within utterance
###   speaker        speaker                  Speaker label (e.g., "Interviewer")
###   text           sentence_text            Sentence text (lowercased)
###   .pred_1        pred_score               Prediction probability (0.0–1.0)
###   context        context                  Surrounding sentences with <main> tags
###
### Note: If the analysis was run before the sentence_prediction feature,
### the endpoint will automatically backfill predictions from the stored
### model_results JSON on first query.
############################################################

